#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:1
msgid "Parse, serialize, and manipulate MIME types"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:3
msgid ""
"This package will parse [MIME types](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org"
"/#understanding-mime-types) into a structured format, which can then be "
"manipulated and serialized:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:25
msgid ""
"Parsing is a fairly complex process; see [the "
"specification](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#parsing-a-mime-type) "
"for details (and similarly [for "
"serialization](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#serializing-a-mime-"
"type))."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:27
msgid ""
"This package's algorithms conform to those of the WHATWG [MIME Sniffing "
"Standard](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/), and is aligned up to "
"commit "
"[8e9a7dd](https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/commit/8e9a7dd90717c595a4e4d982cd216e4411d33736)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:29
msgid "`MIMEType` API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:31
msgid ""
"This package's main module's default export is a class, `MIMEType`. Its "
"constructor takes a string which it will attempt to parse into a MIME "
"type; if parsing fails, an `Error` will be thrown."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:33
msgid "The `parse()` static factory method"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:35
msgid ""
"As an alternative to the constructor, you can use "
"`MIMEType.parse(string)`. The only difference is that `parse()` will "
"return `null` on failed parsing, whereas the constructor will throw. It "
"thus makes the most sense to use the constructor in cases where "
"unparseable MIME types would be exceptional, and use `parse()` when "
"dealing with input from some unconstrained source."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:37
msgid "Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:39
msgid ""
"`type`: the MIME type's [type](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-"
"type-type), e.g. `\"text\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:40
msgid ""
"`subtype`: the MIME type's [subtype](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org"
"/#mime-type-subtype), e.g. `\"html\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:41
msgid ""
"`essence`: the MIME type's [essence](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org"
"/#mime-type-essence), e.g. `\"text/html\"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:42
msgid ""
"`parameters`: an instance of `MIMETypeParameters`, containing this MIME "
"type's [parameters](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type-"
"parameters)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:44
msgid ""
"`type` and `subtype` can be changed. They will be validated to be non-"
"empty and only contain [HTTP token code "
"points](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#http-token-code-point)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:46
msgid "`essence` is only a getter, and cannot be changed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:48
msgid ""
"`parameters` is also a getter, but the contents of the "
"`MIMETypeParameters` object are mutable, as described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:50
msgid "Methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:52
msgid "`toString()` serializes the MIME type to a string"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:53
msgid ""
"`isHTML()`: returns true if this instance represents [a HTML MIME "
"type](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#html-mime-type)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:54
msgid ""
"`isXML()`: returns true if this instance represents [an XML MIME "
"type](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#xml-mime-type)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:55
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"`isJavaScript({ prohibitParameters })`: returns true if this instance "
"represents [a JavaScript MIME "
"type](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/scripting.html#javascript-"
"mime-type). `prohibitParameters` can be set to true to disallow any "
"parameters, i.e. to test if the MIME type's serialization is a "
"[JavaScript MIME type essence match](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org"
"/#javascript-mime-type-essence-match)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:57
msgid ""
"_Note: the `isHTML()`, `isXML()`, and `isJavaScript()` methods are "
"speculative, and may be removed or changed in future major versions. See "
"[whatwg/mimesniff#48](https://github.com/whatwg/mimesniff/issues/48) for "
"brainstorming in this area. Currently we implement these mainly because "
"they are useful in jsdom._"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:59
msgid "`MIMETypeParameters` API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:61
msgid ""
"The `MIMETypeParameters` class, instances of which are returned by "
"`mimeType.parameters`, has equivalent surface API to a [JavaScript "
"`Map`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-"
"US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Map)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:63
msgid ""
"However, `MIMETypeParameters` methods will always interpret their "
"arguments as appropriate for MIME types, so e.g. parameter names will be "
"lowercased, and attempting to set invalid characters will throw."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:65
msgid "Some examples:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:90
msgid "Raw parsing/serialization APIs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:92
msgid ""
"If you want primitives on which to build your own API, you can get direct"
" access to the parsing and serialization algorithms as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:99
msgid ""
"`parse(string)` returns an object containing the `type` and `subtype` "
"strings, plus `parameters`, which is a `Map`. This is roughly our "
"equivalent of the spec's [MIME type "
"record](https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/#mime-type). If parsing fails, "
"it instead returns `null`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/whatwg-mimetype_README.md:101
msgid ""
"`serialize(record)` operates on the such an object, giving back a string "
"according to the serialization algorithm."
msgstr ""

